# Backtest v2 – implementation conventions (read-only survey)

**Scope.** Branch `backtest-v2` @ `f62f68c`. The working tree was clean before and after (the only command run in the repo was `node --test`). Evidence is `repo-path:line`. `db/...` means the live snapshot folder `C:\Users\kadir\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\c--Users-kadir-OneDrive-Masa-st--Wawe-Journal-astro\97ee93d7-3b56-4094-909f-8a419fcb57d4\scratchpad\db`. I ran a few more read-only catalog/aggregate queries on `backtest_trades` and saved the results in `C:\Users\kadir\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\c--Users-kadir-OneDrive-Masa-st--Wawe-Journal-astro\97ee93d7-3b56-4094-909f-8a419fcb57d4\scratchpad\agents\` (`bt_policies.json`, `bt_cols2.json`, `bt_idx.json`, `bt_con.json`, `bt_count.json`). To check the API and the license text, I downloaded the Lightweight Charts 4.1.3 `README.md` and `dist/typings.d.ts` from jsDelivr into `C:\Users\kadir\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\c--Users-kadir-OneDrive-Masa-st--Wawe-Journal-astro\97ee93d7-3b56-4094-909f-8a419fcb57d4\scratchpad\agents\lwc413\`. The detailed rules with citations are in `conventions[]`. This report gives the overview, the hazards and the documentation drift.

## Must-follow checklist

1. **Page shell.** Use `src/pages/backtest.astro` with `<Layout lang='tr' spa={true} ...>`. Head-slot order: page CSS, then CDN libs (the exact LWC URL below, and supabase-js 2.117.3 before `/config.js`), then `/config.js`, then `/i18n.js`, then `<script type='module' src='/src/bundle.js'>`, and finally the page script with `is:inline defer data-page-script` and a `?v=`. Put page assets in `public/interface/backtest/{js,css}/`; that path skips the service-worker cache. Pass `title` to Layout, because BaseHead's `<title>` comes first. Do not add a second `/styles.css` or a legacy `<nav>`.
2. **Lifecycle.**
   - Put all code in an IIFE, with no top-level `const` or `let` in classic scripts, and start with `var PAGE = window.wwPage.current()`.
   - Add window and document listeners only through `PAGE.on`.
   - In `PAGE.onLeave`, release:
     - every replay `setInterval`, `setTimeout` and rAF;
     - every ResizeObserver and MutationObserver;
     - the chart (`chart.remove()`);
     - the expanded viewer (`WwChartViewer.close()`);
     - every node appended to `document.body`.
   - After every `await`, check `if (!PAGE.alive) return`.
   - Prefix element ids with `bt-`.
3. **Boot.** Start from the readyState/DOMContentLoaded check, then poll for `LightweightCharts`, `sb`, `requireAuth` and `journal`. Then call `await requireAuth()` and `await window.journal.ensureActiveJournal(user.id)`.
4. **Charts.** Create charts with `LightweightCharts.createChart(el, WwChart.lwc({...}))` and take candle colours from `WwChart.colors().up/down`. Build hover cards with `WwChart.tipHtml`. Rebuild charts when the theme changes, using a MutationObserver on `body.class`. Resize with a ResizeObserver plus `applyOptions`, or with 4.1.3's `autoSize`. Open the large view with `WwChartViewer.open`, the centered modal.
5. **The TradingView attribution link is required and missing everywhere today** (dashboard, premium-dashboard and the old backtest). Version 4.1.3 has no `attributionLogo` option, so add an HTML link.
6. **Dark mode = `#000`** with neutral hairlines `rgba(255,255,255,0.07-0.1)`. Light mode is white. The generic `.modal-box` is not black: override it the way `strategies.css:1067-1072` does. Show numbers in DM Sans with `tabular-nums`, not JetBrains Mono or DM Mono. Do not use lock icons for premium gating (user preference).
7. **i18n.**
   - Use `data-i18n*` attributes and keep Turkish fallback text in the markup.
   - Add new flat `backtest.*` keys to `en/tr/de`, then bump the `?v` at `i18n.js:126`.
   - Re-render in `PAGE.onI18nChange`.
   - After injecting HTML, call `i18n.apply()` and `lucide.createIcons()`.
8. **Data.** Keep simulated trades out of `trades` unless every reader is changed (section 9). No wwCache prefix may start with `trades`. If a trade is ever promoted into `trades`:
   - set `journal_id` explicitly;
   - send an upper-case direction and an explicit `pnl`;
   - give a non-null `lot` and leave `position_id` NULL;
   - use a namespaced `import_hash` and a `platform_source` tag;
   - then dispatch window `trade-saved`.
9. **Migrations.**
   - Use a new unique version (`20261018NNNN_...`).
   - Keep the usual header and `BEGIN/COMMIT`, and make all DDL idempotent.
   - Create four RLS policies with `user_id = auth.uid() OR public.is_admin()`.
   - Grant RPCs with `REVOKE ALL ... FROM public; GRANT EXECUTE ... TO authenticated`.
   - Migrations are applied by hand in the SQL Editor. Check the live catalog first, because the repo does not match live.
10. **Tests.** Write the engine as a pure IIFE (`window.WwBacktest`), or as an ES module with no DOM or Supabase access at load time. Add `tests/<module>.test.js` loaded through `vm`. Run `node --test tests/*.test.js`, not `tests/`.

## 1. App page structure, SPA and lifecycle

- **Layout** (`src/layouts/Layout.astro:7-80`) renders, in order:
  - BaseHead, then the head slot;
  - the app-page prop scripts;
  - SpaRouter, when `spa` is set;
  - Navbar plus the page slot, both inside `#app-scroll-container`;
  - UpgradeModal, onboarding.js, navbar.js and page-transition.js.
- **BaseHead** (`src/components/BaseHead.astro`) loads, for every app page:
  - fonts (164);
  - `/styles.css?v=` (167) and navbar.css (168);
  - `/cache.js` (171), `time-settings.js` (174) and `trade-metrics.js` (177);
  - chart-theme.css, chart-theme.js and chart-viewer.js (180-182);
  - journal-mark.js (185) and Lucide 0.441.0 (189-190);
  - `/buttons.css` (203);
  - the pre-paint theme, plan and language scripts (206-325).
- **Page assets** follow `strategies.astro:12,32` and `dashboard.astro:460`. `data-page-script` makes SpaRouter re-insert and re-run the script on every visit (`SpaRouter.astro:226-229, 347`). Other `src` scripts run once per tab. Every tag uses `is:inline`.
- **CDN.** Lightweight Charts is loaded from exactly `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/lightweight-charts@4.1.3/dist/lightweight-charts.standalone.production.js`: `dashboard.astro:442`, `premium-dashboard.astro:23`, and the old `backtest.astro:184,186`. If two pages ask for different URLs of the same jsDelivr package, SpaRouter falls back to a full reload (`SpaRouter.astro:92-101,127-140`). The URL must therefore be identical.
- **Caching.**
  - Cloudflare uses must-revalidate (`public/_headers:9-16`).
  - The service worker serves root-level files cache-first, but always goes to the network for `/interface/`, `/components/`, `/src/`, `/settings/` and `*.html` (`public/sw.js:31-63`).
  - So `/i18n.js`, `/config.js`, `/cache.js` and the locale files can be one visit stale unless their `?v` changes.
- **wwPage** (`BaseHead.astro:52-113`) provides `on`, `onLeave`, `expose`, `onI18nChange` and `alive`. SpaRouter calls `wwPage._next()` before every swap (`SpaRouter.astro:299-305`). Cleanup examples:
  - `backtest.astro:435-442` and `559-569` (replay interval and chart);
  - `strategies.js:1944-1957`;
  - `admin-data.js:100-110` (realtime channels and polling);
  - `premium-dashboard.js:810-825`;
  - `dashboard.js:3322-3325`.
- **SpaRouter run order** (`SpaRouter.astro:368-454`):
  1. blocking scripts;
  2. deferred and module scripts;
  3. the captured DOMContentLoaded and load listeners;
  4. `i18n.apply()`;
  5. `lucide.createIcons()`;
  6. the document event `ww:page-load`.
- **What re-runs.** `readyState` is faked while scripts run. Inline scripts re-run on every visit. Module scripts run only once per tab; premium-dashboard mounts again on `ww:page-load` (`premium-dashboard.js:851-869`).
- **What this means for page code:**
  - wrap code in an IIFE;
  - add global listeners only through `PAGE.on`;
  - check `PAGE.alive` after awaits, because ids are reused across pages;
  - use refresh tokens for overlapping loads (`dashboard.js:2990-3003`);
  - use window flags for once-per-tab work (`navbar.js:1760-1763`);
  - publish hooks with `PAGE.expose` (`calendar.js:1217-1218`, `journals.astro:2230`).
- **Auth.** `requireAuth()` (`public/src/core/supabase.js:78-139`) redirects to `login.html`. With `?test=1` and no session it returns a fake user (109-111), so never write with that user. The boot polling pattern is in `dashboard.js:3318-3375`.

## 2. Charts (WwChart, Lightweight Charts usage, viewer)

**WwChart.lwc** (`public/interface/shared/chart-theme.js:154-177`) deep-merges these defaults with the caller's options:
- a transparent background;
- axis text `#c9c9d6` (dark) or `#475569` (light) in 12 px DM Sans;
- horizontal grid lines only;
- a dashed muted crosshair with a `#000` or `#fff` label;
- no scale borders.

It does **not** set the size, `localization`, scroll or scale handling, or series colours. Colours are read at call time (`colors()` 19-32), so charts must be recreated when the theme flips. dashboard.js does this through a body-class MutationObserver (3184-3195), and so does premium-dashboard.js (92-102).

**Gotcha:** `isLight()` reads `document.body`, but BaseHead copies `light-theme` onto `<body>` only at DOMContentLoaded (`BaseHead.astro:276-293`). That is why `dashboard.js:12-22` and `strategies.js:23` start with `initTheme()`.

